            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Engraving and Illustration</strong><br>\nIn addition to his poems and paintings, Blake was highly skilled in engraving and printmaking. He innovated a relief etching technique, which he used to print most of his poetry, calling the method \"illuminated printing.\"</p>\n\n<p><strong>Later Years and Influence</strong><br>\nIn his later years, Blake's work began to gain recognition, and he was commissioned to create illustrations for Dante's \"Divine Comedy.\" He continued to work until his death in 1827.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy</strong><br>\nAfter his death, Blake's influence grew, and he is now regarded as a seminal figure in the history of poetry and the visual arts, with his work inspiring countless artists and writers who followed.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
